// Where word a of copy k (mbase = k << 20) lives (the layout rework, 2026-10-31): a set of pc.ncopy copies (its exact
// copy and the N*N upscaling ones) takes pc.ncopy * 4 MB from word (k - k % pc.ncopy) << 20. Its exact copy is its first
// 4 MB, as before; the upscaling copies follow interleaved, word a of copy c (1 .. N*N) at a * N*N + c - 1, so the copies
// of a word lie side by side and the invocations of a workgroup (one small area in all copies) read and write them
// together. A full-screen pass in scratch/perf/layoutbench: x4 0.115 -> 0.051 ms, x6 0.558 -> 0.125 ms (RTX 5090).
uint va_b, va_s;
void set_va(uint mbase) {
    uint nc = uint(pc.ncopy), k = mbase >> 20, c = k % nc, sb = (k - c) << 20;
    if (c == 0u) { va_b = sb; va_s = 1u; } else { va_b = sb + (1u << 20) + c - 1u; va_s = nc - 1u; }
