        // that shuffle channels through 16-bit views draw 8-pixel strips with gaps, and moving those strips by under a
        // pixel left a column out at one edge and wrote one too many at the other in half the copies (dark lines every
        // 16 pixels, fixed on the screen). Each copy does the same operation on its own memory, unmoved.
